bic_trace_step.reason:
The probe function in this commit adds new rsu_send_msg() calls (for DCMF version and max retry) without returning after calling stratix10_svc_free_channel() on error. For example, lines:

	ret = rsu_send_msg(priv, COMMAND_RSU_DCMF_VERSION, 0, rsu_dcmf_version_callback);
	if (ret) {
		dev_err(dev, "Error, getting DCMF version %i\n", ret);
		stratix10_svc_free_channel(priv->chan);
	}
	ret = rsu_send_msg(priv, COMMAND_RSU_RETRY, 0, rsu_retry_callback);
...

If the first rsu_send_msg fails (e.g., -ETIMEDOUT), the channel is freed but the code continues to the next rsu_send_msg, which will dereference the freed channel (NULL pointer). This matches the described vulnerability root cause.
